<p><font face="helvetica,arial" size="4" color="000000"><b>The New Chardok</b></font></p>
<p align="justify"><font face="helvetica,arial" size="2" color="000000"><b>I would like to thank the 28 players that fought their hearts out on the Chardok raid, Saturday, November 10th. I was very impressed by your diligence and concentration, as well as your patience during downtimes, not to mention the excellent team work that was displayed by a group of players who, some of which, had never met each other before. You fought like we had been friends for years :)
<br><br>
The loot was not what I had expected, even though I, (Bobmd, 56 Luminary), won a pretty nice shoulder piece, (Chokidai Hide Spaulders, 8ac, 8wis, 5svd,m,p). I was hoping to see more of the courageous raiders go home with a nice items for themselves. 
<br><br>
Some of the other items which dropped on the raid were an Argent Defender, 33dmg, 49dly, +20mana, which would probably result in some high damage hits, (won by an awesome pally named Gil...), and a Jagged Chokidai Spine, 9dmg, 25dly, +4 Dex, Poker, (won by Wwen, a SoD ranger).  Annoly waltzed away with a brand new necklace, given to her, not easily, by an angry sarnak, called a Sarnak Arcane Fetish, +2Dex, +5Cha, +6Int. By the way, Annoly rolled a perfect 500 on that item. Congratulations to you three on your exciting new items. (If I missed any other items, I apologize in advance.)
<br><br>
The teamwork was outstanding and the new coalition fought like clockwork, as we took down one mob after another, making it look easy.
<br><br>
After about 3 pulls, Sleastack, (51 Monk from BH) was starting to warm up, and Nocsonnamoon, (52 Warrior also from BH), the main assist, was tagging like a champion!
<br><br>
I have to admit, I made the decision to move the raid party deep inside Chardok, and I was scared. I had never been past the zone in/out camp, and I didn't know what to expect further in the dark, decripit castle, home of the meanest sarnaks in all of Norrath.
<br><br>
On our first attempt to move the raid party deeper into the castle, we discovered 20 or so raiders, from another guild, fighting hard to keep their camp, just inside the castle. We opted to abandon our journey, and retreated back to the zone out camp, to further discuss our plans to advance.
<br><br>
Upon further discussion, we decided to make another attempt at forging forward, as the zone out camp was proving too easy for the valiaint fighters that were among the coalition.
<br><br>
We packed up our tents and gathered our loot, and moved forward, past the guild who was fighting just inside the castle doors. The tanks went first, and cleared the way for the more fragile casters, who helped dismiss any agro, with their powerful damaging spells, from a safe distance. <br><br>
We found a bridge, just down the hall from the castle doors, and made our way across it, without any agro. There was a group camping the bridge, which might have helped :)
<br><br>
As we ventured deeper into the chasm, we discoverd another bridge, the bridge of death, with a long drop on both sides, and frightening mobs crawling around as far as the eye could see. We stopped there, and I approached a mob carefully, who was standing at the entrance to the bridge. I hailed the "bridge keeper". He said, "You must answer me, these questions three, then the other side you'll see!" I replied, "I'm not afraid bridge keeper, ask me the five questions", "Three sir!", butted Kluuvan, "Yes, the three questions", I corrected myself.
<br><br>
"What is your name?", said the bridge keeper. "Bobmd, guild leader of SoD", I replied. "What is your quest?" asked the bridge keeper. "I seek the holy grail", I replied. "What is your favorite color?", he asked. "Why... that's easy...BLUE!... NO, YELLOW!" A loud bang, and a swift whooosh blew me over the bridge, and down into the dark, bottomless pit, never to be seen again. <br><br>
"Kluuvan was next to hail the bridge keeper... Or wait, maybe this was a movie I saw? ;p
<br><br>
All kidding aside, what really happened as we approached the bridge was as follows...
<br><br>
We steadied ourselves on a thin plateau, as the monk pulled, the warrior tagged, and we fought bravely as the mobs continued to drop without incident. I almost lost my life as we found ourselves up against 3 reanimated dragons, which quad for 150. Being a shaman, I can't take too many of those.
<br><br>
In any event, I was saved from certain peril by a last minute heal from 2 of the raiders, in perfect timing, thanks to you both for your timely deed. 
<br><br>
NEXT, we decided to cross the bridge and we quickly found ourselves at the feet of an Ancient Guardian, which conned yellow to me, (56 Shaman), and red to most of the others. We stepped up the attack and he never knew that hit him. Unfortunately, he didn't drop anything nice, but that fight was one to remember for sure.
<br><br>
At this moment, we had had too much fun for any guild alliance, and we decided that we were going to port out safely, before something bad happened. I doubt that anything bad could have happened to a diligent fighting force like the one we had together, but some of the power hitters had to log. Group 3 ported out first, followed closely by group 2, and finally group 1 escaped.
<br><br>
I predict that the coalition will have a chance to participate on more interesting and beneficial raids in the near future. I look forward to hunting with all my new friends again soon.
<br><br>
Bobmd Cureall<br>
Luminary of 56 Winters<br>
Guild Leader - SoD!</b></font></p>

